title: "Bridle: AI Coding Governance Methodology"
message: "If you reference this methodology, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: ghbvf
    family-names: ghbvf
    affiliation: Bridle Project
repository-code: "https://github.com/ghbvf/bridle"
url: "https://ghbvf.github.io/bridle/"
abstract: >-
  Bridle is an engineering governance methodology for the AI-coding era,
  built on three architectural layers (L0 gravity field, L1 state visible,
  L2 intent expressible, L3 autonomous loop) and three paradigm leaps,
  with a six-tier reversibility gradient (R0-R5) that delegates
  reversible actions to AI agents while keeping humans in charge of
  irreversible ones. Integrates the Harness Five-Pack, declarative
  manifests, reconciliation loops, and DORA measurement — letting AI
  code autonomously without losing the organization's grip on its assets.
keywords:
  - AI coding governance
  - autonomous agents
  - Harness engineering
  - declarative manifest
  - reconciliation
  - reversibility gradient
  - DORA
  - software architecture
  - LLM engineering
